{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Sing to Him</b> — on account of the two [words], as if written 'play well to Him with a shout,' in the manner of: 'El, in Your anger rebuke me' [Psalm 6:1]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The argument concerns a two-word phrase treated as if it stands for a single idea; the comparison to Psalm 6:1 involves an analogous grammatical phenomenon, here left cryptic as Ibn Ezra gives it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:16.899779538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}